{#- The capture flow, shared by /help/, /switch-to-openinflowwww/ and /download/. Permissions come from
    loginExtensionMulti/manifest.json; the names from the manifest and the Creators page card. -#}
<p>
  Capturing a session means signing in to the creator's OnlyFans once, so the dashboard can use that login. The creator
  cannot paste it themselves: the Creators page is owner-only. They need Chrome on a computer, not a phone. They install
  the extension (open <code>chrome://extensions</code>, turn on Developer mode, click Load unpacked and pick the
  <code>loginExtensionMulti</code> folder the owner sends them), log in on onlyfans.com, open Messages, click Copy
  curl, and send the copied text to the owner over a channel they would trust with their password. The owner pastes it
  on the Creators page. No password is shared. The copied text is a live login to their account, so treat it like one.
</p>
<p>
  In <code>chrome://extensions</code> it is listed as "Inflowwww Login Capture (OF + Fansly)"; the Creators page card calls
  it "Chatterly Login Capture". Both are old names of the same extension. On the Creators page, from a computer (the
  card is hidden on phones), ignore the Install Chrome Extension button, paste the copied text into the Paste cURL card
  and click Bootstrap from cURL.
</p>
<p>
  The folder is <a href="{{ site.repo }}/tree/main/loginExtensionMulti"><code>loginExtensionMulti/</code></a> at the top
  of the repository. Its manifest asks Chrome for access to onlyfans.com and fansly.com only, and for permission to
  read those sites' cookies, see the open tabs, run its scripts on those sites, keep its own settings and write to the
  clipboard. Remove the extension after the capture.
</p>
